> **Hiring Committee**  
> Sesame Workshop  
> [Workshop Address]  
> [City, State, Zip]  
> 
> Dear Hiring Committee,
> 
> I am writing to express my enthusiastic interest in the Chief Development Officer position at Sesame Workshop, as advertised. As a parent deeply appreciative of the profound impact that Sesame Street has had on my children's educational and emotional development, I am especially excited about the opportunity to contribute to an organization that aligns so closely with my values and aspirations for a better world.
> 
> Sesame Street has not only been a source of joy and entertainment for my sons but has also served as a vital educational tool that has fostered their curiosity, empathy, and foundational skills. The characters and stories resonate meaningfully with young audiences, and I have seen firsthand how they help my children navigate complex emotions and social interactions. The warmth, diversity, and inclusivity that define Sesame’s mission have enriched their early learning experiences and shaped their understanding of kindness and community.
> 
> In my previous roles, I have successfully built and scaled philanthropic initiatives that mirror the mission-driven focus of Sesame Workshop. With a strategic builder's mindset, I have led major gifts campaigns that resulted in increased donor engagement and sustainable revenue streams. I am adept at working cross-functionally, as my experience has equipped me to navigate complex organizational structures while ensuring that philanthropic messaging is coherent and aligned with institutional priorities. 
> 
> I believe that storytelling is a powerful tool for inspiring donors and engaging the community. In my approach, I prioritize crafting compelling narratives that articulate the essential role philanthropy plays in advancing educational initiatives, much like the impactful stories that Sesame Workshop has shared over the years. I aim to help communicate why a trusted brand like Sesame remains indispensable in nurturing the next generation’s growth.
> 
> As someone who values collaboration and believes in nurturing teams, I am committed to cultivating a culture of trust and high performance within the organization. I recognize the importance of empowering leaders and engaging with trustees to unlock new networks and opportunities for collaboration, ensuring that Sesame Workshop can continue its transformative impact on children around the globe.
> 
> I am eager to bring my experience in strategic fundraising, relationship building, and organizational leadership to Sesame Workshop, propelling its mission forward in this pivotal time of transformation. I truly resonate with the belief that every child deserves access to quality educational resources, and I would be honored to contribute to Sesame's vision of making meaningful learning experiences available to families everywhere.
> 
> Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my experience can further Sesame Workshop’s mission and deepen its philanthropic growth.
> 
> Warmest regards,
> 
> James Rising  
